   - First element: `R.compose(R.length, R.prop(1))` - gets the length of the second element
   - Second element: `R.prop(0)` - gets the first element

2. **`R.compose(R.reverse, ...)`** - Reverses the order of comparison so that:
   - The first element is compared first (primary sort)
   - The length of the second element is compared second (secondary sort)

3. **`R.sortBy`** - Sorts the items using the composed comparison function

